s vulnerability assessment and penetration testing by an external firm, which is a narrower scope than a full ''Information Systems audit'', although it is performed annually."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-13","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The control describes an ''internal audit of KYC'' by ''Internal Audit'', which differs from an ''Information Systems audit'' by an ''independent auditor''."},{"control_key":"C-IT-07","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The control describes daily data backup and quarterly restoration testing, which is not an ''Information Systems audit'' and does not involve an independent auditor."}]}]}', 'gemini#2', 'gemini-2.5-flash', 1003, 2385, '2026-10-08 00:24:53.618426+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('71936cb3eb4087e30b547c3315caf77fdf2523e2e6cd1e2a6522e807278e96c1', 'evidence_assessment', '{"verdicts":[{"criterion_id":"K1","verdict":"MET","evidence_id":"858037eb-bff5-4b3b-b25d-2a062efb9401","quote":"Critical patches released in the period: 40. Applied within 14 days: 21. Applied within 30 days: 34. Applied after 30 days: 6.","rationale":"The excerpt provides a summary of patch application data, which is consistent with information found in patch management logs.","confidence":1.0},{"criterion_id":"K2","verdict":"MET","evidence_id":"858037eb-bff5-4b3b-b25d-2a062efb9401","quote":"Critical patches released in the period: 40. Applied within 14 days: 21. Applied within 30 days: 34. Applied after 30 days: 6.","rationale":"The excerpt provides a summary of system update status for critical patches, which serves as a system update report.","confidence":1.0}]}', 'gemini#2', 'gemini-2.5-flash', 473, 804, '2026-10-08 00:25:02.005929+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('a0917366c27f015cb5c1f60ddeadc817fd2b5e8372f812edfe4b219bdfec2b6b', 'evidence_assessment', '{"verdicts":[{"criterion_id":"K1","verdict":"MET","evidence_id":"706fb87b-2717-4f5a-b283-a56c97c84e6b","quote":"Vulnerability assessment and penetration test of 18 critical systems.","rationale":"The evidence explicitly states that a vulnerability assessment and penetration test was conducted, indicating the existence of related reports.","confidence":1.0},{"criterion_id":"K2","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT","evidence_id":null,"quote":null,"rationale":"The excerpt mentions an ''agreed closure date'' but does not explicitly state that management signed off on the VA/PT results.","confidence":0.8},{"criterion_id":"K3","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT","evidence_id":null,"quote":null,"rationale":"The provided excerpt does not contain any information about an Information Systems audit report.","confidence":1.0},{"criterion_id":"K4","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT","evidence_id":null,"quote":null,"rationale":"The excerpt does not include an engagement letter or contract with an independent auditor.","confidence":1.0}]}', 'gemini#2', 'gemini-2.5-flash', 496, 762, '2026-10-08 00:25:16.553548+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('05681011a1b5e75a6396f2dd7c40506e45d16f479a99581dbc27c713aa81bbf6', 'evidence_assessment', '{"verdicts":[{"criterion_id":"K1","verdict":"MET","evidence_id":"7d18d9b4-0d77-4842-9d9f-10b319b7cb93","quote":"Quarterly review of user access rights for 12 critical systems has been completed.","rationale":"The evidence explicitly states that the quarterly review of user access rights has been completed, which serves as a record of the review.","confidence":0.9}]}', 'gemini#2', 'gemini-2.5-flash', 459, 493, '2026-10-08 00:25:29.794244+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('d133a09b21018dff6c0192237cd4af2f9001e2597ab634ed03444052c72710be', 'evidence_assessment', '{"verdicts":[{"criterion_id":"K1","verdict":"MET","evidence_id":"979ab205-9478-465d-892f-abb24737fe7f","quote":"Log source PAM-01 retention policy: 180 days hot storage. Log records include user identifiers and source IP addresses.","rationale":"The evidence indicates that PAM logs, which are associated with privileged access, include user identifiers and source IP addresses, demonstrating system logs of privileged access sessions.","confidence":0.9},{"criterion_id":"K2","verdict":"MET","evidence_id":"979ab205-9478-465d-892f-abb24737fe7f","quote":"Log source PAM-01 retention policy: 180 days hot storage.","rationale":"The evidence explicitly states the log retention policy for PAM logs is 180 days hot storage.","confidence":0.9},{"criterion_id":"K3","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT","evidence_id":null,"quote":null,"rationale":"While the evidence mentions ''hot storage'', it does not explicitly confirm the storage location is the SIEM or provide details about retrieval capabilities.","confidence":0.7}]}', 'gemini#2', 'gemini-2.5-flash', 476, 785, '2026-10-08 00:25:47.39844+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('cbfb302c8df5bb2c9a1d270e58be1afc76c9e76650580969cd1a69b8ffec8670', 'remediation', '{"plans":[{"finding_id":"95c03584-feac-4f24-af96-056fa9e31ab5","root_cause":"There is no formal process or control established to ensure that a root cause analysis is conducted for every critical incident, leading to a complete lack of coverage for the incident management obligation.","actions":[{"kind":"POLICY_UPDATE","description":"Draft and approve a new Incident Management Policy section requiring a formal root cause analysis (RCA) for all critical incidents, defining scope, responsibilities, and timelines."},{"kind":"PROCESS_CHANGE","description":"Design and document a new incident management process flow for critical incidents, detailing the steps for initiating, conducting, documenting, and reviewing RCAs."},{"kind":"CONTROL_CHANGE","description":"Create a new control (e.g., C-INC-01) to monitor the timely initiation and completion of root cause analyses for critical incidents, including review and approval steps."},{"kind":"TECHNOLOGY_CHANGE","description":"Configure the existing Incident Management System (e.g., ServiceNow, Jira Service Management) to include mandatory fields and workflows for critical incident RCA documentation and tracking."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Conduct a pilot test of the new RCA process and control on a simulated critical incident or a recent past critical incident to identify any gaps or inefficiencies."},{"kind":"APPROVAL","description":"Obtain formal approval from relevant stakeholders (e.g., Head of Incident Management, Compliance, Risk) for the new policy, process, and control."}],"suggested_owner":"Head - Incident Management","target_days":120,"dependencies":["Incident Management Team","IT Operations","Compliance Department","Risk Management"],"expected_evidence":"Approved Incident Management Policy update, documented critical incident RCA process, new control C-INC-01 definition, system configuration screenshots, and completed RCA reports for critical incidents.","verification_method":"Review the updated Incident Management Policy and process documentation. Sample critical incident records to verify that a root cause analysis was conducted and documented according to the new process and control.","touches_production":true},{"finding_id":"30c8e37e-ddf4-4ddc-8c12-2f927f25dcf2","root_cause":"The existing control C-IT-04 is designed to deploy critical security patches within 30 days, which directly conflicts with the obligation''s 14-day requirement. Additionally, the control''s monthly frequency and outdated evidence indicate a failure in timely execution and monitoring.","actions":[{"kind":"POLICY_UPDATE","description":"Update the IT Security Patching Policy to explicitly mandate the application of critical security patches to all critical systems within 14 days of their release."},{"kind":"CONTROL_CHANGE","description":"Modify control C-IT-04 to align with the 14-day patching deadline for critical systems and adjust its monitoring frequency to at least bi-weekly to ensure timely compliance."},{"kind":"PROCESS_CHANGE","description":"Revise the critical security patching process to include an expedited, out-of-band patching cycle for critical vulnerabilities, ensuring deployment within the 14-day window, independent of the standard monthly cycle."},{"kind":"TECHNOLOGY_CHANGE","description":"Evaluate and upgrade the Patch Server and associated automation tools to support faster patch deployment, more frequent scanning, and real-time reporting capabilities to meet the 14-day deadline."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Implement automated, continuous collection of patch compliance reports for critical systems, demonstrating that critical patches are applied within 14 days of release."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Conduct a re-test of control C-IT-04 and the revised patching process to confirm that critical security patches are consistently applied to critical systems within 14 days."}],"suggested_owner":"Head - IT Operations","target_days":90,"dependencies":["IT Security Team","System Administrators","Change Management Team"],"expected_evidence":"Updated IT Security Patching Policy, revised control C-IT-04 documentation, updated critical patching process documentation, automated patch deployment reports showing 14-day compliance, and successful control re-test results.","verification_method":"Review the updated policy and control documentation. Sample critical systems'' patch logs and deployment reports to verify that critical security patches are consistently applied within 14 days of release. Review control re-test results.","touches_production":true}]}', 'gemini#2', 'gemini-2.5-flash', 767, 2606, '2026-10-08 00:26:06.159127+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('bac475985775137b8152ff1d0ecf8c609755b147cfd406c616c701cb7fc9e7a4', 'remediation', '{"plans":[{"finding_id":"2a1b7265-be92-421f-894f-61aa1eee309f","root_cause":"Control C-IT-07 is flagged as not operating effectively despite existing daily backup schedules, indicating potential failures in daily execution, backup job logging, or partial coverage of critical data in Backup System.","actions":[{"kind":"TECHNOLOGY_CHANGE","description":"Review and reconfigure automated daily backup job schedules and alert thresholds for all critical data repositories within the Backup System."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Execute a comprehensive test run of daily backup jobs across all critical data targets and verify successful completion."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Collect 14 consecutive days of daily backup success logs and job completion reports from the Backup System."},{"kind":"APPROVAL","description":"Submit backup job completion records to Head - IT Operations for review and formal operational sign-off."}],"suggested_owner":"Head - IT Operations","target_days":30,"dependencies":["Database Administration Team","Infrastructure Engineering Team"],"expected_evidence":"Automated job execution logs demonstrating successful daily backups of all critical data for 14 consecutive days and signed operational review sign-off.","verification_method":"Compliance inspection of daily backup execution logs from Backup System and verification of alert configurations for failed jobs.","touches_production":true},{"finding_id":"97d05d55-8fc0-4b29-bec4-9dfb3dc3eacf","root_cause":"Lack of documented control testing and absence of formal evidence collection artefacts proving continuous MFA enforcement by the Identity Provider and PAM for privileged users.","actions":[{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Extract configuration exports and policy enforcement rules from Identity Provider and PAM showing mandatory MFA for all privileged user groups."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Perform an operating effectiveness test sampling privileged access sessions across critical systems to verify MFA challenges are enforced."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Export authentication audit logs for the tested sample demonstrating successful multi-factor authentication prompt and completion."},{"kind":"APPROVAL","description":"Review testing results and policy configurations with CISO and obtain formal sign-off on operating effectiveness."}],"suggested_owner":"CISO","target_days":15,"dependencies":["IT Department","IAM / PAM Operations Team"],"expected_evidence":"Identity Provider and PAM configuration documentation confirming continuous MFA enforcement, along with sample audit logs verifying successful MFA challenges for privileged users.","verification_method":"Compliance review of PAM/IdP MFA configuration baselines and independent sample testing of privileged authentication logs.","touches_production":false}]}', 'gemini#4', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 796, 942, '2026-10-08 00:26:32.804207+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('e1f0f0bb3d2e208fe570b279970efe69200ea41d1a5582544574b3537029892d', 'remediation', '{"plans":[{"finding_id":"2aa8d324-e272-4890-8c23-a946b1fd900e","root_cause":"Control C-IT-04 evidence collection lapsed past the 30-day monitoring window (currently 48 days old) alongside a failed control test, compounded by an underlying process alignment issue where C-IT-04 operates on a monthly (30-day) cycle while the obligation requires critical patching within 14 days.","actions":[{"kind":"PROCESS_CHANGE","description":"Update the patch management standard operating procedure to align critical security patch timelines from 30 days to within 14 days of release."},{"kind":"TECHNOLOGY_CHANGE","description":"Reconfigure Patch Server scheduling rules to detect and deploy critical security patches within the 14-day SLA."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Perform end-to-end patch deployment testing across critical test systems to address and resolve recent test failures."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Extract and submit fresh patch deployment logs and compliance reports from Patch Server confirming patch installation within 14 days."}],"suggested_owner":"Head - IT Operations","target_days":14,"dependencies":["IT Security","System Administrators","Change Advisory Board"],"expected_evidence":"Patch Server deployment completion reports showing critical patches deployed within 14 days and test pass status.","verification_method":"Compliance re-audit of Patch Server deployment timestamp logs and verification of patch currency against vendor release dates.","touches_production":true},{"finding_id":"c5dd18ec-cc0a-4d7d-ab4f-42a314333ced","root_cause":"Control C-IT-05 is designed with an annual frequency (P1Y) instead of the mandated semi-annual frequency (P6M), resulting in 313-day-old testing evidence that fails the required 180-day cycle.","actions":[{"kind":"POLICY_UPDATE","description":"Revise Business Continuity and DR policy to mandate critical system DR drills at least once every six months (P6M)."},{"kind":"CONTROL_CHANGE","description":"Update control C-IT-05 schedule and frequency attribute from P1Y to P6M in the internal controls register."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Schedule and conduct an immediate disaster recovery drill for critical systems at the DR Site to cure the overdue cycle."},{"kind":"APPROVAL","description":"Submit the DR drill results and failover evaluation report to the IT Strategy Committee for formal approval."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Upload the IT Strategy Committee approved DR drill report and failover logs to the compliance evidence repository."}],"suggested_owner":"Head - IT Operations","target_days":45,"dependencies":["IT Strategy Committee","Business Continuity Management Team","Infrastructure Engineering"],"expected_evidence":"Minutes of IT Strategy Committee reviewing the DR drill report and signed DR Site drill test execution logs conducted within the last 180 days.","verification_method":"Compliance inspection of the semi-annual DR drill schedule and review of the IT Strategy Committee meeting minutes and test report.","touches_production":true}]}', 'gemini#4', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 874, 1603, '2026-10-08 00:26:47.459254+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('6a7bd3d16e61463d07638eb155e2552e658d71df884423b384fd90294e4b211f', 'remediation', '{"plans":[{"finding_id":"6102645c-e62f-4442-9e36-a66da0bf4bea","root_cause":"Absence of a formal governance control and reporting framework establishing direct reporting of the Chief Information Security Officer to the Executive Director or equivalent.","actions":[{"kind":"POLICY_UPDATE","description":"Update the Information Security Governance Charter and reporting structure to explicitly mandate direct reporting of the CISO to the Executive Director or equivalent."},{"kind":"APPROVAL","description":"Submit the revised reporting structure and governance charter to the Board or Executive Director for formal sign-off."},{"kind":"CONTROL_CHANGE","description":"Create and map a new internal compliance control (e.g. C-GOV-CISO-REP) to enforce and monitor the CISO direct reporting line."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Collect updated organisational charts, signed job descriptions, and reporting minutes demonstrating CISO direct reporting."}],"suggested_owner":"Chief Information Security Officer","target_days":30,"dependencies":["Human Resources","Executive Directorate","Corporate Governance"],"expected_evidence":"Approved Information Security Governance Charter and verified organisational chart confirming the CISO reports directly to the Executive Director.","verification_method":"Compliance review of the approved governance charter, organisational reporting line documentation, and committee minutes.","touches_production":false},{"finding_id":"0a1ece36-c5c3-4e07-8a45-8f6413c80bf8","root_cause":"Lack of a defined board-level control establishing and maintaining the constitution of the IT Strategy Committee of the Board.","actions":[{"kind":"POLICY_UPDATE","description":"Draft the Terms of Reference and Charter for the constitution of the Board IT Strategy Committee."},{"kind":"APPROVAL","description":"Present and obtain Board approval for the establishment and membership constitution of the IT Strategy Committee."},{"kind":"CONTROL_CHANGE","description":"Institute a formal governance control (e.g. C-GOV-ITSC-CONST) tracking the active constitution and regular convening of the IT Strategy Committee."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Compile signed Board resolutions and the approved IT Strategy Committee Charter as baseline compliance evidence."}],"suggested_owner":"Company Secretary / Board Secretariat","target_days":45,"dependencies":["Board of Directors","Chief Technology Officer / CIO","Legal and Compliance"],"expected_evidence":"Signed Board resolution approving the constitution of the IT Strategy Committee and its formal Terms of Reference.","verification_method":"Inspection of Board meeting minutes, signed constitution resolution, and Committee charter by the Compliance team.","touches_production":false}]}', 'gemini#4', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 651, 889, '2026-10-08 00:26:54.352627+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('bfac19b0439447ce2e4957d283c6014427e4a9bf8c6ad01c2c5288819cfc4550', 'remediation', '{"plans":[{"finding_id":"e643478d-0173-474f-afd1-c2e6b2c4d604","root_cause":"Absence of a documented control or defined governance process mapping the obligation to submit the report to the Board within 30 days.","actions":[{"kind":"POLICY_UPDATE","description":"Draft and incorporate a mandatory reporting procedure requiring the report to be placed before the Board within 30 days of completion."},{"kind":"CONTROL_CHANGE","description":"Create and register a new governance control in the compliance framework establishing recurring tracking and scheduling of the report on the Board agenda."},{"kind":"APPROVAL","description":"Submit the newly designed governance control and reporting timeline to the Board Secretariat and Compliance Head for formal approval."}],"suggested_owner":"Company Secretary / Board Secretariat","target_days":25,"dependencies":["Board Secretariat","Compliance Department"],"expected_evidence":"Approved control documentation and Board meeting pack/minutes demonstrating submission within 30 days.","verification_method":"Compliance audit of Board agenda dates against report issuance dates to confirm adherence to the 30-day SLA.","touches_production":false},{"finding_id":"9776fe29-32b9-4b00-b53b-264279e90d32","root_cause":"Evidence artefacts for control C-IT-07 have not been refreshed in the compliance repository, leading to stale verification data despite control execution.","actions":[{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Collect recent daily backup execution logs and latest quarterly restoration test results for critical systems from the Backup System."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Validate the retrieved daily backup logs and quarterly restoration records against control C-IT-07 requirements."},{"kind":"PROCESS_CHANGE","description":"Establish a recurring monthly evidence submission workflow from the Backup System to the compliance repository for C-IT-07."}],"suggested_owner":"Head - IT Operations","target_days":14,"dependencies":["IT Operations","Backup Administrators"],"expected_evidence":"Fresh daily backup logs and documented quarterly restoration test reports from the Backup System.","verification_method":"Compliance review of submitted daily backup logs and quarterly test sign-off documentation.","touches_production":false}]}', 'gemini#4', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 722, 1709, '2026-10-08 00:27:08.304135+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('4da90bb10652b83ff651287d6232517a42c6b68df87b0b581a7221b6798c40d9', 'evidence_assessment', '{"verdicts":[{"criterion_id":"K1","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT","evidence_id":null,"quote":null,"rationale":"The provided evidence describes onboarding workflow rules and does not contain any information regarding the appointment of a Data Protection Officer.","confidence":1.0},{"criterion_id":"K2","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT","evidence_id":null,"quote":null,"rationale":"The provided evidence does not contain any employment documentation or details about the DPO''s location.","confidence":1.0},{"criterion_id":"K3","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT","evidence_id":null,"quote":null,"rationale":"The provided evidence does not contain data deletion or purging logs.","confidence":1.0},{"criterion_id":"K4","verdict":"INSUFFICIENT","evidence_id":null,"quote":null,"rationale":"The provided evidence does not contain a data retention and disposal policy.","confidence":1.0}]}', 'groq#2', 'qwen/qwen3.8-27b', 714, 322, '2026-10-08 00:28:46.474228+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('be79527bcbe969cc54523ec05dca51d526d018b7920c09c0cd244d763be13097', 'obligation_verification', '{"results":[{"candidate_id":"Candidate 0","entailed":true,"reason":"The source text clearly mandates that a data fiduciary must erase personal data within three years of account closure unless required by law."},{"candidate_id":"Candidate 1","entailed":true,"reason":"The source text states that personal data in system and application logs shall not be retained for more than 90 days."},{"candidate_id":"Candidate 2","entailed":true,"reason":"The source text requires a data fiduciary to notify the Authority of any personal data breach within 72 hours of awareness."},{"candidate_id":"Candidate 3","entailed":true,"reason":"The source text stipulates that a data fiduciary must conduct data protection awareness training annually for employees handling personal data."},{"candidate_id":"Candidate 4","entailed":true,"reason":"The source text explicitly requires a data fiduciary to appoint a Data Protection Officer based in India."}]}', 'gemini', 'gemini-3.5-flash-lite', 629, 283, '2026-10-08 00:27:53.433803+00', 1, '2026-10-08 05:42:56.502147+00', NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('94176a41cc7462fc8dc6218b40e4a7e46a8d0e893a05debb49f25f153bc146b8', 'control_mapping', '{"mappings":[{"obligation_id":"obligation 2.1","judgements":[{"control_key":"C-KYC-08","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.95,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The obligation mandates erasure of customer personal data no later than three years after account closure, whereas C-KYC-08 is a retention control keeping records for five years and does not provide for erasure within three years."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-09","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-KYC-09 covers STR filing with the FIU and does not address data erasure or retention timelines."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-04","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-KYC-04 pertains to beneficial ownership identification during onboarding and does not address data erasure after account closure."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-03","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-KYC-03 concerns CDD and identity verification during onboarding, with no coverage of account closure or data erasure."}]},{"obligation_id":"obligation 2.2","judgements":[{"control_key":"C-IT-03","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.95,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The obligation caps log retention containing personal data at 90 days, whereas C-IT-03 retains privileged session logs for 180 days, exceeding the required limit."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-08","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-KYC-08 covers five-year archival of transaction and customer identification records, not log retention limits of 90 days."},{"control_key":"C-IT-02","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-IT-02 governs quarterly user access reviews and revocation, which does not relate to log retention periods."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-09","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-KYC-09 governs STR filing workflows, having no relevance to system/application log retention."}]},{"obligation_id":"obligation 3.1","judgements":[{"control_key":"C-KYC-09","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-KYC-09 addresses STR filings with the FIU within seven working days, not personal data breach notification to the Authority."},{"control_key":"C-IT-08","relation":"PARTIAL","coverage":0.5,"confidence":0.85,"control_quote":"The Security Operations Centre classifies incidents and reports cyber security incidents to the regulator within six hours of detection.","reason":"C-IT-08 has a stricter timeline (six hours vs 72 hours) and reports to a regulator, but its scope is restricted to cyber security incidents rather than all personal data breaches."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-02","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-KYC-02 deals with AML Principal Officer designation and communication within 30 days, not data breach reporting."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-11","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":1.0,"control_quote":null,"reason":"C-KYC-11 handles AML transaction monitoring alerts within 30 days, entirely unrelated to personal data breach notification."}]}]}', 'gemini#4', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 1414, 1255, '2026-10-08 00:28:08.423096+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('79d393601b52abd259e45dfcdb15f71302b6edb1741f0541ce7553d63c9e1961', 'control_mapping', '{"mappings":[{"obligation_id":"4.1","judgements":[{"control_key":"C-KYC-12","relation":"PARTIAL","coverage":0.5,"confidence":0.9,"control_quote":"Annual KYC/AML training. All frontline staff complete KYC and AML e-learning once a year","reason":"Frequency matches annual requirement but scope is limited to frontline staff and content is KYC/AML rather than data protection awareness"},{"control_key":"C-IT-06","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.9,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control describes vulnerability assessment, not training on data protection"},{"control_key":"C-IT-07","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.9,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control concerns backup and restore testing, unrelated to training"},{"control_key":"C-KYC-01","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.9,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control is about policy approval and review, not training"}]},{"obligation_id":"4.2","judgements":[{"control_key":"C-KYC-02","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.9,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control appoints a Principal Officer for AML, not a Data Protection Officer and does not specify location"},{"control_key":"C-KYC-09","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.9,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control describes STR filing workflow, unrelated to DPO appointment"},{"control_key":"C-KYC-03","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.9,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control concerns customer due diligence onboarding, not DPO appointment"},{"control_key":"C-KYC-01","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.9,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control is about KYC policy approval, not DPO appointment"}]}]}', 'groq', 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1274, 1316, '2026-10-08 00:28:28.476928+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
