s record retention periods rather than secure storage controls for V-CIP recordings."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-04","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.95,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control C-KYC-04 concerns beneficial ownership verification and does not address secure storage of recordings."}]},{"obligation_id":"fe9f1a76-793f-4c1b-83a8-fe5c1d688b0f","judgements":[{"control_key":"C-KYC-08","relation":"FULL","coverage":1.0,"confidence":0.95,"control_quote":"Transaction records and customer identification records are archived and retained for five years from the transaction date or from closure of the relationship, whichever is later.","reason":"Control C-KYC-08 retains transaction records for at least five years from the transaction date, fully meeting the obligation scope and duration threshold."},{"control_key":"C-IT-03","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.95,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control C-IT-03 covers privileged access session logs retained for 180 days, not customer transaction records."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-11","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.95,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control C-KYC-11 addresses automated AML transaction monitoring and alert investigation, not transaction record retention."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-09","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.95,"control_quote":null,"reason":"Control C-KYC-09 relates to Suspicious Transaction Report filing workflows rather than maintaining transaction records for five years."}]}]}', 'gemini#3', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 1327, 1464, '2026-10-08 00:43:08.960568+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
