ching the conclusion."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-10","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The control covers monthly Cash Transaction Report (CTR) submissions rather than Suspicious Transaction Reports (STRs)."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-02","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The control handles Principal Officer designation and communication to the FIU, not the filing of STRs within seven working days."},{"control_key":"C-IT-08","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The control concerns cyber incident reporting within six hours and is completely unrelated to STR filing with the FIU."}]},{"obligation_id":"47335c08-741b-4f3a-8e94-7228c25be036","judgements":[{"control_key":"C-KYC-10","relation":"FULL","coverage":1.0,"confidence":0.95,"control_quote":"Cash Transaction Reports are generated from the core banking system every month and submitted to the FIU before the 15th of the following month.","reason":"The control matches the required monthly frequency and submits CTRs to the FIU before the 15th of the following month, fully satisfying the obligation."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-09","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The control governs event-driven Suspicious Transaction Reports (STR) rather than monthly Cash Transaction Reports (CTR)."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-02","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The control relates to designating and notifying the FIU of the Principal Officer, not submitting monthly CTRs."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-11","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"The control addresses internal automated AML transaction monitoring and alert closure within 30 days, not monthly CTR reporting to the FIU."}]}]}', 'gemini#3', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 1451, 1365, '2026-10-08 00:43:27.094516+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('87f8179c74bb50c135281da372733beb9b947ad725bc510660bbc1a23b2e6031', 'control_mapping', '{"mappings":[{"obligation_id":"fe94dbd7-9205-42e0-8d2f-8454a6248127","judgements":[{"control_key":"C-KYC-12","relation":"FULL","coverage":1.0,"confidence":0.98,"control_quote":"All frontline staff complete KYC and AML e-learning once a year; completion is tracked in the learning management system.","reason":"The control matches the target audience (all frontline staff), subject matter (KYC and AML), and required frequency (once a year)."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-01","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"This control pertains to annual Board approval and review of the KYC and AML policy, not staff training."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-05","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"This control addresses customer risk categorisation review, which is unrelated to frontline staff training."},{"control_key":"C-KYC-06","relation":"NONE","coverage":0.0,"confidence":0.99,"control_quote":null,"reason":"This control covers periodic KYC updation tracking for customers, not staff training."}]}]}', 'gemini#4', 'gemini-3.8-flash', 713, 1036, '2026-10-08 00:44:15.441819+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO public.llm_cache VALUES ('20739987aff77092af82a288ff0bda605be8566ccd67b4a2804fe27e0ede1075', 'remediation', '{"plans":[{"finding_id":"15e76a09-c302-4abf-93fe-f6dcc2209349","root_cause":"The bank lacks a formal SOP and automated trigger to ensure the Principal Officer appointment is communicated to the FIU within 30 days, causing reliance on ad‑hoc manual actions and incomplete evidence of compliance.","actions":[{"kind":"POLICY_UPDATE","description":"Update the AML Reporting Policy to explicitly require FIU notification of Principal Officer appointment within 30 days and define responsible roles."},{"kind":"PROCESS_CHANGE","description":"Create a Standard Operating Procedure (SOP) with a checklist and deadline tracking for the appointment notification process."},{"kind":"TECHNOLOGY_CHANGE","description":"Configure the compliance workflow system to auto‑generate a FIU notification task and escalation alerts when a new Principal Officer is entered in the HR system."},{"kind":"CONTROL_CHANGE","description":"Amend control C‑KYC‑02 to require a signed notification log and quarterly audit of FIU acknowledgements."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Collect and archive FIU acknowledgment receipts for each appointment as part of the compliance evidence repository."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Perform quarterly testing of the notification workflow, verifying that all appointments are reported within the 30‑day window."}],"suggested_owner":"Chief Compliance Officer","target_days":60,"dependencies":["IT Compliance Systems Team","HR System Owner","FIU Liaison"],"expected_evidence":"Updated AML Reporting Policy, SOP document, workflow configuration screenshots, signed notification logs, quarterly test reports.","verification_method":"Internal audit will compare appointment dates from HR records to FIU acknowledgment timestamps and review test results for any missed deadlines.","touches_production":true},{"finding_id":"801fb026-e013-4f09-b3b4-0c0fedac8106","root_cause":"The current monthly tracker and 60‑day branch completion window do not guarantee that high‑risk customers are re‑validated within the required two‑year period, resulting in delayed KYC refreshes and incomplete coverage.","actions":[{"kind":"POLICY_UPDATE","description":"Revise the KYC Refresh Policy to mandate completion of high‑risk customer KYC within 24 months of the flag, not merely 60 days after flagging."},{"kind":"PROCESS_CHANGE","description":"Redesign the monthly tracker process to issue a 30‑day reminder and automatic escalation if the KYC update is not completed."},{"kind":"TECHNOLOGY_CHANGE","description":"Enhance the Core Banking System to auto‑close KYC tasks after 24 months and provide a compliance dashboard showing overdue high‑risk updates."},{"kind":"CONTROL_CHANGE","description":"Update control C‑KYC‑06 to require a signed off KYC completion record and evidence that the update occurred within the two‑year deadline."},{"kind":"EVIDENCE_COLLECTION","description":"Archive completed KYC documents with system timestamps for all high‑risk customers as proof of timely refresh."},{"kind":"TESTING","description":"Conduct semi‑annual compliance testing to sample high‑risk customers and verify KYC was refreshed within the 24‑month window."}],"suggested_owner":"Head of Retail Operations / KYC Compliance Lead","target_days":90,"dependencies":["Core Banking IT Team","KYC Operations Team","Data Analytics Team"],"expected_evidence":"Revised KYC Refresh Policy, updated SOP, system dashboard screenshots, signed KYC completion records, semi‑annual test reports.","verification_method":"Compliance audit will sample high‑risk customer records, compare the last KYC refresh date to the flag date, and confirm the update occurred within 24 months; test reports will be reviewed quarterly.","touches_production":true}]}', 'groq', 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 1150, 1536, '2026-10-08 00:46:26.190485+00', 0, NULL, NULL);
